{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Audit - Application - Unauthorized Access to an Okta Application",
	"Description": "Someone tried to reach an Okta application they are not assigned to. A handful of these are users clicking stale bookmarks; a burst from one account or one address is enumeration of what the org has published.\n\nEvent type: app.generic.unauth_app_access_attempt\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
